WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.810
I have good news and bad news to start with
today, and therefore same depending on your

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:06.810
perspective.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:11.510
Donald Trump last night gave what is likely
to be his last rally ever as president of

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:12.590
the United States.

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:15.580
If you like the Trump craziness, it's coming
to an end.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.720
If you dislike it, it's coming to an end.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.220
So it's good or bad, depending on your perspective.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.400
It was bizarre.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.400
It was deranged.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.029
It was also really boring.

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:26.279
And it took place in Georgia.

00:00:26.279 --> 00:00:31.329
The point of the rally supposedly was to support
the two Republican senators running in today's

00:00:31.329 --> 00:00:34.000
elections, Kelly Lefler and David Perdue.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.300
But down to every detail, the entire event
was a farce.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:44.280
David Perdue couldn't even be at the rally
because he's in coronavirus quarantine.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:49.740
Of the nearly 90 minutes that Donald Trump
ranted, almost none of it was about the Senate

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:50.740
candidates.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:54.440
It was mostly about Trump, much of it telling
lie after lie.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:59.520
It is not an exaggeration to say Donald Trump
told hundreds of lies during yesterday's rally,

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.729
insisting he won at one point simply citing
supposed county level vote count numbers from

00:01:04.729 --> 00:01:05.729
election night.

00:01:05.729 --> 00:01:10.719
The crowd completely silent for long stretches
of the rally and down to the last element.

00:01:10.719 --> 00:01:14.900
I mean, even Trump's face more orange than
we've ever seen it.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:19.990
Despite his pale hands, every detail could
not have been more absurd and as I like to

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:24.039
say, indistinguishable from satire.

00:01:24.039 --> 00:01:25.950
So let's get right into it.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:30.250
Here is Donald Trump within seconds opening
up the rally by lying about the results in

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:31.250
Georgia.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.259
I want to thank you very much.

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:33.259
Hello, George.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:36.560
By the way, there's no way we lost Georgia.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.380
This no rig.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:41.409
That was a rigged election.

00:01:41.409 --> 00:01:43.439
So we're still fighting it.

00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:44.869
And you'll see what's going to happen.

00:01:44.869 --> 00:01:46.319
We'll talk about it.

00:01:46.319 --> 00:01:48.009
And and this was the theme.

00:01:48.009 --> 00:01:52.899
Trump moments later saying, if Democrats take
the White House and then realizing, hold on

00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:53.899
a second.

00:01:53.899 --> 00:01:55.189
No, no, no, they're not taking it.

00:01:55.189 --> 00:01:56.189
We won.

00:01:56.189 --> 00:02:00.939
If the liberal Democrats take the Senate to
the White House and they're not taking this

00:02:00.939 --> 00:02:03.130
White House, we're going to fight like hell.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:06.450
I'll tell you right now.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:13.160
And the theme was that the crowd really didn't
seem to care very much about Lefler and Purdue,

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:17.250
they seemed to just be there for Trump.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.920
But even Trump got too boring for them for
long stretches.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:26.450
And they tuned out, which will get to Donald
Trump, then alluding to once again hoping

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:31.810
that Mike Pence can steal the election for
him tomorrow.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:36.000
And I hope Mike Pence comes through for us.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:42.170
I have to tell you, I hope that our great
vice president, our great vice president comes

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:43.170
through for us.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:49.560
He's a great guy because if he doesn't come
through, I won't like him quite as much.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.520
So this is wild for two reasons.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:57.750
First, that Donald Trump is publicly pressuring
the vice president to steal the election.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:04.270
And second, that Donald Trump seems to believe
that Mike Pence can steal the election.

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:10.800
Pence's role in Washington, D.C. tomorrow,
as we talked about yesterday, is really perfunctory.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.680
And we're all going to see that tomorrow.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:14.910
So I won't get get ahead of myself.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:18.600
Here is an example of Donald Trump ranting
about things nobody in the crowd seemed to

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:19.600
understand.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:20.600
And the crowd is silent.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.560
At one point I wondered, did the crowd leave?

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.600
But they were they're just not making a peep.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.690
And you've got to swarm it tomorrow.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:32.010
Now, the good thing about tomorrow, it's one
stage.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.560
So you have a lot of eyeballs watching.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:40.010
It's tougher than when you have 50 states
and they do it to various various states.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:42.070
I never said they like it.

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:47.080
I was leading in Pennsylvania by hundreds
of thousands of votes.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.100
All of a sudden I was tired.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:50.340
I said, what happened?

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:58.150
They'll make Washington, D.C. and other liberal
places the 50 first, 50 second, 50 third states

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:03.240
of the union, guaranteeing you can almost
hear the room tone louder than you can hear

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.240
the crowd.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:09.060
It's really wild how dead silent Trump was
able to get this crowd to be.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:14.510
Trump then defiantly clarifying he does not
concede, even though he did lose two months

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:15.510
ago.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:18.760
After all, nothing and no one will be able
to stop them.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:24.260
These Senate seats are truly the last line
of defense.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:28.610
Now, I must preface that by saying because
they'll say he just conceded.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:33.390
No, no, I don't think so.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:38.250
That got the crowd awake, Trump not conceding
that's the one thing he should be doing and

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:41.050
mentioning that is what really gets the crowd
fired up.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:43.030
So then this is funny.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:47.210
When Donald Trump did talk about David Perdue
and Carly Lefler, which was almost not at

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:49.350
all, but that was the point of the rally.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:53.540
In theory, the crowd is totally bored when
Trump talks about Perdue and Lefler.

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:57.460
Here he is talking about David Perdue, who
it wasn't even clear whether Trump knew Perdue

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:59.680
wasn't there because he was quarantining.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:00.680
Doesn't matter.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:03.020
You'll see the camera if you're watching pan
around.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:07.940
And although the lack of masks is notable,
the lack of enthusiasm is as well.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:14.040
Over the last four years, David Perdue has
been one of our greatest allies and strongest

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.530
defenders in Washington.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:17.530
He's a great gentleman.

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:23.450
And then the crowd just as bored when Trump
was talking about Carly Lefler, just barely

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:24.620
a cheer.

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:30.300
Georgia has another fantastic champion and
Senator Kelly Lefler.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:34.760
Kelly is a staunch defender of our incredible
military.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:36.300
I'm so proud of our military.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:42.460
She supports the war and she always stands
with the heroes of law enforcement ICE.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:45.669
Usually they pump up the crowd noise.

00:05:45.669 --> 00:05:48.610
I was wondering whether they were suppressing
the crowd noise.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:49.610
And that's a joke.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:50.610
They weren't.

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:53.570
The crowd was just that silent for much of
this rally.

00:05:53.570 --> 00:05:56.770
A deflated, empty speech, the cringe.

00:05:56.770 --> 00:06:03.139
Yes, moment in the whole thing was probably
this moment when Donald Trump called up Republican

00:06:03.139 --> 00:06:08.330
Senate candidate Carly Lefler to the stage
and she had an announcement to make, which

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:15.110
was that tomorrow she will object, object
to the counting of the electoral votes that

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:16.540
got the crowd interested.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.300
They woke up for that.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.470
Hello, Georgia.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:23.730
Thank you, George.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:31.220
I have an announcement, Georgia, on January
6th, I will object to the Electoral College

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.320
vote.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.520
That's right.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:36.730
Thank you.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:41.970
What energy, right, I mean, just the energy
just oozing off of Kelly Lefler there, loudly

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:47.830
announcing she will also be making a fool
out of herself in Washington, D.C. tomorrow.

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:53.000
And Trump then seemed to be visibly struggling
to get to the end of his speech.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:57.050
You're going to hear him sort of slurring
here, mixing up words.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:04.380
The last 20 minutes were just one of the most
poorly delivered speeches that I've seen from

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:05.380
Trump, and that says a lot.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:10.169
We've all seen what our opponents are capable
of doing.

00:07:10.169 --> 00:07:12.450
I ran to elections.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:15.120
I won both of them.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:19.110
Second one, much more successful than the
first.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:23.449
But we can't let this happen any longer on
election night.

00:07:23.449 --> 00:07:24.970
We were leading by so much.

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:26.530
We're not going to have that tomorrow.

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:32.400
So then this is the part that's really nuts
for about 20 straight.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:40.699
And it's Trump Red with terrible inflection
in tone, alleged voting results from various

00:07:40.699 --> 00:07:41.699
counties.

00:07:41.699 --> 00:07:46.430
And here he is wanting to talk about Maricopa
County, Arizona, but he's only only able to

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:48.430
get out the word Mayakoba.

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:51.490
And it doesn't even matter because everybody's
tuned out by this point anyway.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:57.419
So his constituents reported that their earlier
in-person ballots may not have been correctly

00:07:57.419 --> 00:07:58.550
processed or tabulated.

00:07:58.550 --> 00:07:59.550
And Maricopa County officials.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:00.550
Yes.

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:06.009
So this was the part that had the crowd completely
checked out, just droning on like this for

00:08:06.009 --> 00:08:07.009
20 minutes.

00:08:07.009 --> 00:08:08.040
Here's another part of it.

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:10.259
You could really hear a pin drop in this place.

00:08:10.259 --> 00:08:16.009
The committee then heard additional testimony
concerning voting irregularities during the

00:08:16.009 --> 00:08:22.169
2020 general election, including testimony
and a real time test demonstrating serious

00:08:22.169 --> 00:08:25.830
irregularities with Dominion's voting machines.

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:31.280
Three events discussed at this hearing stand
out and require a forensic order of the Dominion

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:36.760
voting machines in Georgia to be immediately
conducted.

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:42.580
The one phrase that woke people back up was
Trump mentioning Dominion voting machines.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:47.100
The sycophants have almost been trained in
a Pavlovian manner.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:49.820
If you hear dominion that you have to react
to.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:54.880
But they were really struggling to remain
even remotely engaged with Trump droning on

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.980
and on about votes and ballots.

00:08:56.980 --> 00:09:02.860
And then during his wind up sort of crescendo,
Trump actually glitches on the word America

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:06.150
and he tries to cover it up by flexing his
bicep.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:10.850
We have made America stronger again.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:13.580
Look at that.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:14.700
Trump commonly does this.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:19.870
We saw this dozens and dozens of times during
his presidency when he sort of glitches out

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.130
during a word.

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:23.230
He'll do something physical to distract from
it.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:27.070
He'll flex his arm or he'll slap the lectern
a couple of times, or he'll turn to the other

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:30.190
side of the audience and say, whoa, hey, how
about that?

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:35.000
So Trump's final rally, as expected, all about
himself.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:40.430
He seemed sort of to try to go through the
motions of talking about David Perdue and

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:42.610
Carly Lefler, but he really couldn't do it.

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:46.810
And what he did do is spend a lot of time
claiming that he won in November.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:50.529
We are very close to the end, very, very close.

00:09:50.529 --> 00:09:56.200
And the next question is, what will Trump
do between tomorrow when the electoral votes

00:09:56.200 --> 00:10:00.320
are counted and January 20th when Joe Biden
is sworn in?

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.320
Will we see him at all?

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:03.580
Will he tweet?

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.070
Will he go crazy tweeting?

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:06.810
Will he not tweet at all?

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:07.830
We don't know.

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:15.320
But you can join me tonight live on YouTube,
Twitch and Facebook for Georgia Senate results

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:18.980
starting somewhere in the 7:00 p.m. Eastern
hour.

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:24.310
And then tomorrow at 1:00 p.m. Eastern, join
me live on YouTube, Twitter and Facebook for

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:30.779
the counting of the electoral votes, supposedly
the last stand for the Trump.

00:10:30.779 --> 00:10:32.890
That's tomorrow, 1:00 p.m. Eastern.

00:10:32.890 --> 00:11:47.019
Join me tonight and join me tomorrow.

